    90	for interrupt handling, followed by cleanup. Startup (roughly 240 seconds
    91	maximum health probing), builds, pulls and collection are outside that budget.
    92	Schemathesis status 1 is retained as a testing outcome if a JUnit report exists;
    93	JUnit and text logs must still be reviewed for test errors versus assertions.
    94	Budget expiry is an incomplete run and exits nonzero; JUnit/cassette may be
    95	unfinished, while stdout remains available. Raise the common budget or lower
    96	the common example limit and rerun all conditions if complete runs are needed.
    97	
    98	Each `E1_pilot/runs/scout-api/<run_id>/` holds:
    99	
   100	- `run.json`: all seven arguments, effective example/body limits, paths, auth
   101	  assumption, timestamps, return codes, EMB commit/dirty status, SHA-256 hashes,
   102	  image IDs and registry digests when present. Local SUT builds usually have
   103	  an image ID without `RepoDigests`; that is recorded explicitly.
   104	- Original and tested spec snapshots; mutated runs also have `mutation/`,
   105	  `manifest.json`, `specmut.log` and the exact generator input.
   106	- `exchanges.jsonl`, `schemathesis.log`, JUnit XML and cassette when flushed;
   107	  exact generator arguments, saved CLI help, resolved compose and inspection JSON.
   108	- `jacoco.exec`, dump log, Compose logs, cleanup logs and health evidence.
   109	
   110	The EXIT/INT/TERM handler removes only this run's named generator, dumps
   111	coverage while the SUT is alive, then tears down only this Compose project.
   112	There is no system prune or volume deletion. JaCoCo's CLI dump is the documented
   113	way to retrieve TCP-server execution data
   114	([official dump command](https://www.jacoco.org/jacoco/trunk/doc/cli.html)).
   115	Coverage failure, empty exchanges or teardown failure marks the run incomplete.
   116	SIGKILL, host loss or Docker daemon loss cannot guarantee cleanup; use the
   117	saved project name and resolved compose to inspect and clean up that project.
   118	Do not infer successful completion from directory existence alone.
   119	
   120	## Assumptions and review gates for T7
   121	
   122	- **Health:** `/admin/healthcheck` through port 8080 is an inference from
   123	  `scout_api_evomaster.yml:5-10` and `ScoutAPIApplication.java:146-147` (under
   124	  `jdk_8_maven/cs/rest/original/scout-api/api/src/main/java/se/devscout/scoutapi/`).
   125	  ⚠️ Its actual HTTP route and proxy behavior remain unverified. A non-2xx
   126	  response fails readiness. Override `HEALTH_PATH` only after confirming it.
   127	- **Base path:** `/api` is declared in `openapi-swagger/scout-api.json:11` and
   128	  `scout_api_evomaster.yml:5`; the v3 `--base-url` handling must be checked
   129	  against actual captured request paths, especially doubled or missing `/api`.
   130	- **Authentication:** spec has no security declaration, but
   131	  `ScoutAPIApplication.java:186-203` registers auth filters, and
   132	  `auth/src/main/java/se/devscout/scoutapi/auth/apikey/ApiKeyAuthenticator.java:17`
   133	  declares `ApiKey`. Config seeds `user`, `moderator`, `administrator`
   134	  identities (`scout_api_evomaster.yml:54-75`). ⚠️ Unauthenticated coverage may
   135	  be limited. This batch deliberately records auth=`none`; a confirmed auth
   136	  experiment needs a separate documented configuration and reruns of controls.
   137	- **Logger errors (T4 S03):** T10 owns `tools/mitm_fulllog.py`. T10/T7 should
   138	  provide and verify an `error(flow)` hook for upstream timeout/reset, recording
   139	  request + correlation ID + transport error even without a response. Add that
   140	  hook in the logger, not this harness. Keep failed flows distinct from HTTP
   141	  violations; reconcile attempted/generated requests, response exchanges,
   142	  transport failures and truncated bodies before interpreting coverage.
   143	  T5 has not changed the logger and does not assert that this hook exists.
   144	- **Inference limits:** fresh analysis uses baseline traffic/original oracle
   145	  versus mutated traffic/mutated oracle (`--mode fresh`); NEW/VANISHED are
   146	  observational and need manual causal review. Replay evaluates **the same
   147	  baseline exchange records**, first with the original, then mutated spec
   148	  (`--mode replay`); it sends no HTTP requests and isolates checker/oracle
   149	  differences. It cannot measure generation-side harm of REQUEST_LOOSE or
   150	  REQUEST_STRICT. See `09_collab/reports/T4_review.md:R03,S03` from research/.
   151	- **Runtime checks:** UID/GID permissions, image entrypoint/flags, health route,
   152	  base-path behavior, JVM/agent compatibility, TCP dump and proxy flushing are
   153	  integration questions. T5 only supplies static validation. Fixed seeds do
   154	  not make stateful fuzzing or fresh runs identical; baseline seeds 1–3 help
   155	  observe variation but do not prove causal attribution.

